            },
            {
               "text": "#### *PICHANA* (inverse)\n\n*PICHANA* means \"broom\" in Quechua. In addition, the *PICHANA* movement sweeps markers together from squares 1 and 2 into square 3. In subtraction, we reverse this broom. Two cases appear here: when a marker is in square 3 (value 3) and we need to subtract 2, or when a marker is in square 2 (value 2) and we need to subtract 1. In the first case, the inverse movement decomposes the 3 into three unit markers in square 1 (1 + 1 + 1 = 3) and removes two of them, leaving 1. In the second case, it decomposes the 2 into two unit markers in square 1 (1 + 1 = 2) and removes one of them, leaving 1. This represents the operations\n",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a62b520a-f443-4d83-ab51-b99c9a46dab8",
                     "text": "Prem, Dhavit",
                     "page": "pp. 360",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2018",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "1bb0274d-dc51-4740-ac62-4d157b06ad88",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team (2024). Yupana (Addition)",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ":"
