            {
               "text": "### Cancellation\n\nAn important concept in subtraction on the Yupana is **cancellation**. When two markers of the same color occupy the same square, they stand for the same value being both added and subtracted, so they cancel each other out — any number subtracted by itself equals zero. For example, in 5 − 5 = 0 the two markers meet in the same square and leave nothing behind. This principle is especially useful for simplifying calculations during subtraction.\n",
